s moving it out or whatever he  opens up the fridge take the paperwork  and throws it in there and closes it  pushes her back so she goes back into  the warehouse and they all start running  in 30 seconds later the light the  cameras are cut  they cut the cameras  process for me was very scary i'm  thinking like what did we do wrong did  the police come or did the feds come  the feds are usually going to come they  got some [ __ ] if it's the police they  probably are messed up i didn't know for  i didn't know for like 10 hours  our attorney gets there they put him in  handcuffs they didn't care and you know  at the end of the day what they were  there for was something called acid  forfeiture and what that means is if  you're found of any wrongdoing at all  any at all they confiscate everything  and they get to keep it so if there's a  million dollars in the building if  there's five luxury cars on the property  whatever they get to keep all of it if  you're found for doing any wrongdoing  six employees that was there they all  did uh jail they were in jail for four  days which is the max amount of time you  can be there without being charged they  couldn't find anything to charge them  for for the four days but they made them  stay the entire four days it was really  emotional for them like honestly man um  they're all still very traumatized  behind that  episode like if you talk to my aunt  about it uh and you know when our  growers they'll break down crying every  time they can't even have a conversation  about it without  crying you know what i'm saying it  brings them back to a very dark place  that obviously it just wasn't cool so we  went through the process had to get each  one of them they're all attorneys and  long story short went in court and they  threw it out and they said they had no  business rating us you know not only did  we have  um authorization from the city we  authorization from the state which  nobody in the state had at that time we  were 